\" cc\", leaving space before b? Wait: \"aaa b cc\" -> removing \" cc\" (positions? careful: after previous steps, text was \"aaa b cc\". \" cc\" at indices 5,6,7? Actually \"aaa b cc\" -> characters: a a a space b space c c. Indices: 0 a,1 a,2 a,3 space,4 b,5 space,6 c,7 c. \" cc\" is space at 5, c at6, c at7? No \" cc\" is space + c + c? But there are two c's. So \" cc\" matches space then two c's. So indices 5,6,7. Replace with empty string => removes these three characters, leaving \"aaa b\". That is a a a space b -> \"aaa b\". So text becomes \"aaa b\". Now sweep2:\n\nPass halve-a: old \"aa\" in \"aaa b\". First occurrence of \"aa\" at indices 0-1? \"aaa\" -> \"aa\" at 0,1. Replace with \"a\" -> \"a\" + rest from index2 (\"a b\") => \"aa b\"? Actually \"aaa b\": indices0 a,1 a,2 a,3 space,4 b. Replace first \"aa\" (0-1) with \"a\" -> new string: \"a\" + \"a b\" (remaining from index2) => \"aa b\". Change, record \"halve-a\".\n\nPass drop-b: old \"bb\" in \"aa b\". No \"bb\", no change.\n\nPass drop-c: old \" cc\" in \"aa b\". No \" cc\", no change.\n\nSweep2 changed: only halve-a. applications append \"halve-a\".\n\nSweep3: text = \"aa b\". Pass halve-a: old \"aa\" at indices 0-1, replace with \"a\" => \"a b\". Change, record \"halve-a\". Pass drop-b: \"bb\" not present. Pass drop-c: not present. Sweep3 changed.\n\nSweep4: text = \"a b\". Pass halve-a: old \"aa\" not present. Pass drop-b: \"bb\" not present. Pass drop-c: \" cc\" not present. No changes, fixed point reached. total sweeps = 4 (<=8). fixed_point = True. applications = [\"halve-a\",\"drop-b\",\"drop-c\",\"halve-a\",\"halve-a\"]? Wait ordering: Sweep1: halve-a, drop-b, drop-c. Sweep2: halve-a. Sweep3: halve-a. So sequence: halve-a, drop-b, drop-c, halve-a, halve-a. That's 5 entries. Return text = \"a b\". That seems plausible.\n\nBut the output schema says \"applications\" is array of strings, presumably the order of pass names that changed the artifact. The fixture payloads are identical, so result